      "content": "Ammonia buildup in soil can be caused by fungal infections, especially in excess nitrogen-rich fertilizers or heavy rainfall, which allow ammonia to leach into the soil. While it's not a common issue, you can look for yellowing, stunted, or scorched grass around affected areas and actual ammonia smell. However, if your lawn just needs more nutrients, you'll notice slower nutrient deficiencies rather than ammonia-related damage. You can also try the 'iodine test': mix iodine crystals with dew or rainwater, and apply it to the damaged areas - if the grass rapidly turns blue or black, it might indicate an excess of ammonia.",
